{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LowestCommonAncestors","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For vertices at preorder positions p < q, the answer is the vertex at the least position among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parents of the vertices at positions p + 1 … q. Those parents lie in the answer’s subtree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and include it, and it has the least position there. A query is therefore one range minimum"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over n − 1 parent positions, answered by 64-entry blocks with a bitmask of each prefix’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minimum stack and a sparse table over the blocks’ minima. Memory is about 20 bytes per vertex,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plus (n\/64)·log₂(n\/64) entries for the table."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/init(